# Negative control — the panel no longer OPENS on its first declared option: it
# starts in the seed order with nothing applied, which is the unnamed state the
# "Default" entry used to stand for. Every option still sorts once picked, and
# the select still lists them, so the control looks right until you read what it
# says on arrival.
#
# Intended RED: "opens on the first option, and an empty or unknown value falls
# back to it" and "the products listing opens A–Z, and ranks undated one-time
# rows last by renewal" (tests/collection-search-sort.test.ts).

